IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc7-s183-base`
IMPORT `ccc7-s183-offence`
IMPORT `ccc7-s195-notification`

-- ccc7-tests-s195-notification.l4 -- tests for ccc7-s195-notification.l4 (ss 195, 196, 196.1). Expected values are written by hand from the text, beside each assertion.
-- Dates are worked by hand: 1 January 2025 plus 90 days is 1 April 2025 (31 + 28 + 31 = 90 days from 1 January to 1 April); 1 January 2024 plus 90 days is 31 March 2024 (2024 is a leap year).

GIVEN statute IS A `s 183 statute`
      n IS A NUMBER
      sub IS A STRING
GIVETH A `s 183 provision of an Act`
`s 195 test provision` MEANS `s 183 provision of an Act` WITH `statute` IS statute, `section` IS n, `subsection` IS sub

§ `Tests -- section 195`

-- (1) args: a year has ended, the matter, the interceptions relate to an offence for which the Attorney General of Canada may commence proceedings
#ASSERT `s 195(1) the Minister is bound to prepare a report relating to the matter` TRUE `s 195(1)(a) authorizations for which the Minister and agents specially designated by the Minister for the purposes of section 185 applied, and the interceptions made under them in the preceding year` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 195(1) the Minister is bound to prepare a report relating to the matter` TRUE `s 195(1)(b) authorizations given under section 188 for which peace officers specially designated by the Minister applied, and the interceptions made under them in the preceding year` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 195(1) the Minister is bound to prepare a report relating to the matter` TRUE `s 195(1)(c) interceptions made under section 184.4 in the preceding year` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (c) "if the interceptions relate to an offence for which proceedings may be commenced by the Attorney General of Canada"
#ASSERT `s 195(1) the Minister is bound to prepare a report relating to the matter` TRUE `s 195(1)(c) interceptions made under section 184.4 in the preceding year` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a matter the three paragraphs do not name: not covered
#ASSERT `s 195(1) the Minister is bound to prepare a report relating to the matter` TRUE `s 195(1) another matter` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the year has not ended
#ASSERT `s 195(1) the Minister is bound to prepare a report relating to the matter` FALSE `s 195(1)(a) authorizations for which the Minister and agents specially designated by the Minister for the purposes of section 185 applied, and the interceptions made under them in the preceding year` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the duty as a rule: read the traces in NOTES.md
#TRACE `s 195(1) the duty to prepare the annual report as a rule` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 183 the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness` DOES `s 195(1) prepares the annual report` AT 20
-- (2): each of (a) to (n), and an item the list does not name
#ASSERT `s 195(2) the report must set out the item` `s 195(2)(a) the number of applications made for authorizations` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 195(2) the report must set out the item` `s 195(2)(b) the number of applications made for renewal of authorizations` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 195(2) the report must set out the item` `s 195(2)(c) the numbers of those applications that were granted, refused, and granted subject to terms and conditions` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 195(2) the report must set out the item` `s 195(2)(d) the number of persons identified in an authorization against whom proceedings were commenced at the instance of the Attorney General of Canada, by kind of offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 195(2) the report must set out the item` `s 195(2)(e) the number of persons not identified in an authorization against whom proceedings were commenced, by kind of offence, whose offence became known as a result of an interception` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 195(2) the report must set out the item` `s 195(2)(f) the average period for which authorizations were given and renewals granted` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 195(2) the report must set out the item` `s 195(2)(g) the number of authorizations valid for more than sixty, one hundred and twenty, one hundred and eighty and two hundred and forty days` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 195(2) the report must set out the item` `s 195(2)(h) the number of notifications given pursuant to section 196` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 195(2) the report must set out the item` `s 195(2)(i) the offences in respect of which authorizations were given, with the number for each` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 195(2) the report must set out the item` `s 195(2)(j) a description of all classes of places specified in authorizations and the number for each class` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 195(2) the report must set out the item` `s 195(2)(k) a general description of the methods of interception involved in each interception` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 195(2) the report must set out the item` `s 195(2)(l) the number of persons arrested whose identity became known as a result of an interception` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 195(2) the report must set out the item` `s 195(2)(m) the number of criminal proceedings in which intercepted communications were adduced in evidence and the number that resulted in a conviction` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 195(2) the report must set out the item` `s 195(2)(n) the number of criminal investigations in which information was used although the communication was not adduced in evidence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 195(2) the report must set out the item` `s 195(2) an item that is none of those` EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2.1): each of (a) to (j)
#ASSERT `s 195(2.1) the report must set out the item` `s 195(2.1)(a) the number of interceptions made` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 195(2.1) the report must set out the item` `s 195(2.1)(b) the number of parties to each intercepted private communication against whom proceedings were commenced` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 195(2.1) the report must set out the item` `s 195(2.1)(c) the number of persons who were not parties to an intercepted private communication but whose offence became known as a result, and against whom proceedings were commenced` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 195(2.1) the report must set out the item` `s 195(2.1)(d) the number of notifications given under section 196.1` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 195(2.1) the report must set out the item` `s 195(2.1)(e) the offences in respect of which interceptions were made and any other offences for which proceedings were commenced, with the number of interceptions for each` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 195(2.1) the report must set out the item` `s 195(2.1)(f) a general description of the methods of interception used for each interception` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 195(2.1) the report must set out the item` `s 195(2.1)(g) the number of persons arrested whose identity became known to a police officer as a result of an interception` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 195(2.1) the report must set out the item` `s 195(2.1)(h) the number of criminal proceedings commenced in which intercepted communications were adduced in evidence and the number that resulted in a conviction` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 195(2.1) the report must set out the item` `s 195(2.1)(i) the number of criminal investigations in which information was used even though the communication was not adduced in evidence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 195(2.1) the report must set out the item` `s 195(2.1)(j) the duration of each interception and the aggregate duration of all the interceptions related to the investigation of the offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 195(2.1) the report must set out the item` `s 195(2.1) an item that is none of those` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 195(3) the report must set out the item` `s 195(3)(a) the number of prosecutions commenced against officers or servants of Her Majesty in right of Canada or members of the Canadian Forces for offences under section 184 or 193` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 195(3) the report must set out the item` `s 195(3)(b) a general assessment of the importance of interception of private communications for the investigation, detection, prevention and prosecution of offences in Canada` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 195(3) the report must set out the item` `s 195(3) an item that is none of those` EQUALS NOTHING
-- (4) args: Parliament was sitting at completion, laid forthwith, laid on the nth sitting day after completion
#ASSERT `s 195(4) the report was laid before Parliament in time` TRUE TRUE 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 195(4) the report was laid before Parliament in time` TRUE FALSE 1 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not sitting: "on any of the first fifteen days next thereafter that Parliament is sitting": the 15th sitting day is in time, the 16th is not
#ASSERT `s 195(4) the report was laid before Parliament in time` FALSE FALSE 1 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 195(4) the report was laid before Parliament in time` FALSE FALSE 15 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 195(4) the report was laid before Parliament in time` FALSE FALSE 16 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 195(4) the report was laid before Parliament in time` FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (5)
#ASSERT `s 195(5) the Attorney General of each province is bound to prepare and publish a report relating to the matter` TRUE `s 195(5)(a) authorizations for which the Attorney General and agents specially designated by the Attorney General for the purposes of section 185 applied, and the interceptions made under them in the preceding year` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 195(5) the Attorney General of each province is bound to prepare and publish a report relating to the matter` TRUE `s 195(5)(b) authorizations given under section 188 for which peace officers specially designated by the Attorney General applied, and the interceptions made under them in the preceding year` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 195(5) the Attorney General of each province is bound to prepare and publish a report relating to the matter` TRUE `s 195(5)(c) interceptions made under section 184.4 in the preceding year` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 195(5) the Attorney General of each province is bound to prepare and publish a report relating to the matter` TRUE `s 195(5)(c) interceptions made under section 184.4 in the preceding year` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 195(5) the Attorney General of each province is bound to prepare and publish a report relating to the matter` TRUE `s 195(5) another matter` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 195(5) the Attorney General of each province is bound to prepare and publish a report relating to the matter` FALSE `s 195(5)(a) authorizations for which the Attorney General and agents specially designated by the Attorney General for the purposes of section 185 applied, and the interceptions made under them in the preceding year` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Tests -- section 196(1) and (2): the 90 days`

-- the day after a period: add years, then months, then days
#ASSERT `s 196(1) the day after a period that begins on the day` (Date 1 1 2025) (`Length of time` OF 0 , 0 , 90 , FALSE) EQUALS Date 1 4 2025
#ASSERT `s 196(1) the day after a period that begins on the day` (Date 1 1 2025) (`Length of time` OF 3 , 0 , 0 , FALSE) EQUALS Date 1 1 2028
#ASSERT `s 196(1) the day after a period that begins on the day` (Date 15 1 2025) (`Length of time` OF 1 , 2 , 3 , FALSE) EQUALS Date 18 3 2026
-- the last day for notice: the period ends 1 January 2025 -> 1 April 2025; 2024 is a leap year -> 31 March 2024
#ASSERT `s 196(1) the last day for notifying the person who was the object of the interception` (Date 1 1 2025) NOTHING 0 EQUALS Date 1 4 2025
#ASSERT `s 196(1) the last day for notifying the person who was the object of the interception` (Date 1 1 2024) NOTHING 0 EQUALS Date 31 3 2024
-- days of suspension are not counted
#ASSERT `s 196(1) the last day for notifying the person who was the object of the interception` (Date 1 1 2025) NOTHING 10 EQUALS Date 11 4 2025
-- "such other period as is fixed pursuant to subsection 185(3) or subsection (3)": replaces the 90 days
#ASSERT `s 196(1) the last day for notifying the person who was the object of the interception` (Date 1 1 2025) (JUST (`Length of time` OF 3 , 0 , 0 , FALSE)) 0 EQUALS Date 1 1 2028
#ASSERT `s 196(1) the last day for notifying the person who was the object of the interception` (Date 1 1 2025) (JUST (`Length of time` OF 1 , 0 , 0 , FALSE)) 5 EQUALS Date 6 1 2026
-- in time: the last day itself is in time, the day after is not
#ASSERT `s 196(1) the notice was given in time` (Date 1 4 2025) (Date 1 4 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 196(1) the notice was given in time` (Date 31 3 2025) (Date 1 4 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 196(1) the notice was given in time` (Date 2 4 2025) (Date 1 4 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (2): from the day the application was made until the day it was heard and disposed of
#ASSERT `s 196(2) the number of days the running of the period is suspended` (Date 1 2 2025) (Date 11 2 2025) EQUALS 10
#ASSERT `s 196(2) the number of days the running of the period is suspended` (Date 1 2 2025) (Date 1 2 2025) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 196(2) the number of days the running of the period is suspended` (Date 11 2 2025) (Date 1 2 2025) EQUALS 0
-- the duty as a rule (the clock starts the day the period ends = day 0): notice on day 89, certificate afterwards; notice on day 91; nothing at all
#TRACE `s 196(1) the duty to notify the person and certify to the court as a rule` `s 183 the Attorney General of the province` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 183 the Attorney General of the province` DOES `s 196(1) notifies in writing the person who was the object of the interception` AT 89
    PARTY `s 183 the Attorney General of the province` DOES `s 196(1) certifies to the court that gave the authorization that the person has been notified` AT 100
#TRACE `s 196(1) the duty to notify the person and certify to the court as a rule` `s 183 the Attorney General of the province` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 183 the Attorney General of the province` DOES `s 196(1) notifies in writing the person who was the object of the interception` AT 91
#TRACE `s 196(1) the duty to notify the person and certify to the court as a rule` `s 183 the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 183 the Minister of Public Safety and Emergency Preparedness` DOES `s 196(1) notifies in writing the person who was the object of the interception` AT 90
#TRACE `s 196(1) the duty to notify the person and certify to the court as a rule` `s 183 the Attorney General of the province` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 91)

§ `Tests -- section 196(3) to (5)`

-- (3) args: the investigation of the offence is continuing, a subsequent investigation is continuing, the subsequent offence is listed in section 183 (s 183), the interests of justice warrant the granting
#ASSERT `s 196(3) the judge shall grant an extension of the period` TRUE FALSE NOTHING TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 196(3) the judge shall grant an extension of the period` FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (b) requires an offence "listed in section 183"
#ASSERT `s 196(3) the judge shall grant an extension of the period` FALSE TRUE (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 196(3) the judge shall grant an extension of the period` FALSE TRUE NOTHING TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 196(3) the judge shall grant an extension of the period` FALSE FALSE (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not of the opinion that the interests of justice warrant it
#ASSERT `s 196(3) the judge shall grant an extension of the period` TRUE FALSE NOTHING FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 196(3) the extension is within the limit` (`Length of time` OF 3 , 0 , 0 , FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 196(3) the extension is within the limit` (`Length of time` OF 3 , 0 , 1 , FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (4) args: accompanied by an affidavit, (a) facts, (b) the number of instances
#ASSERT `s 196(4) the application meets the requirement of the subsection` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 196(4) the application meets the requirement of the subsection` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 196(4) the application meets the requirement of the subsection` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 196(4) the application meets the requirement of the subsection` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (5) args: satisfied that the investigation is in relation to the offence, the offence, benefit of a group, criminal organization (s 2), terrorism offence (s 2), the opinion that the interests of justice warrant it
-- (a): 52, 52.1, 52.2, 467.11, 467.111, 467.12, 467.13: this list DOES name 467.111
#ASSERT `s 196(5) the judge shall grant an extension of the period` TRUE (`s 195 test provision` `s 183 the Criminal Code` 467.111 "") FALSE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 196(5) the judge shall grant an extension of the period` TRUE (`s 195 test provision` `s 183 the Criminal Code` 467.11 "") FALSE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 196(5) the judge shall grant an extension of the period` TRUE (`s 195 test provision` `s 183 the Criminal Code` 52 "") FALSE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 196(5) the judge shall grant an extension of the period` TRUE (`s 195 test provision` `s 183 the Criminal Code` 380 "") TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 196(5) the judge shall grant an extension of the period` TRUE (`s 195 test provision` `s 183 the Criminal Code` 380 "") FALSE (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- this list has no limb for an offence under the Foreign Interference and Security of Information Act (finding 3)
#ASSERT `s 196(5) the judge shall grant an extension of the period` TRUE (`s 195 test provision` `s 183 the Foreign Interference and Security of Information Act` 20 "(1)") FALSE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 196(5) the judge shall grant an extension of the period` TRUE (`s 195 test provision` `s 183 the Criminal Code` 380 "") FALSE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 196(5) the judge shall grant an extension of the period` TRUE (`s 195 test provision` `s 183 the Criminal Code` 52 "") FALSE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 196(5) the judge shall grant an extension of the period` FALSE (`s 195 test provision` `s 183 the Criminal Code` 52 "") FALSE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 196(5) the judge shall grant an extension of the period` TRUE (`s 195 test provision` `s 183 the Criminal Code` 380 "") TRUE NOTHING (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 196(5) the extension is within the limit` (`Length of time` OF 3 , 0 , 0 , FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 196(5) the extension is within the limit` (`Length of time` OF 3 , 0 , 1 , FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Tests -- section 196.1`

-- (1): the interception occurred on 1 January 2025: last day 1 April 2025; with an extension of one year (added to the 90 days) and 5 days' suspension: 1 April 2026 + 5
#ASSERT `s 196.1(1) the last day for giving notice of the interception` (Date 1 1 2025) NOTHING 0 EQUALS Date 1 4 2025
#ASSERT `s 196.1(1) the last day for giving notice of the interception` (Date 1 1 2024) NOTHING 0 EQUALS Date 31 3 2024
#ASSERT `s 196.1(1) the last day for giving notice of the interception` (Date 1 1 2025) NOTHING 7 EQUALS Date 8 4 2025
#ASSERT `s 196.1(1) the last day for giving notice of the interception` (Date 1 1 2025) (JUST (`Length of time` OF 1 , 0 , 0 , FALSE)) 5 EQUALS Date 6 4 2026
#ASSERT `s 196.1(1) the notice was given in time` (Date 1 4 2025) (Date 1 4 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 196.1(1) the notice was given in time` (Date 2 4 2025) (Date 1 4 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 196.1(2) the number of days the running of the period is suspended` (Date 1 2 2025) (Date 11 2 2025) EQUALS 10
#ASSERT `s 196.1(2) the number of days the running of the period is suspended` (Date 11 2 2025) (Date 1 2 2025) EQUALS 0
#TRACE `s 196.1(1) the duty to give notice of the interception as a rule` `s 183 the Attorney General of the province` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 183 the Attorney General of the province` DOES `s 196.1(1) gives notice in writing of the interception to the person who was the object of it` AT 90
#TRACE `s 196.1(1) the duty to give notice of the interception as a rule` `s 183 the Attorney General of the province` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 183 the Attorney General of the province` DOES `s 196.1(1) gives notice in writing of the interception to the person who was the object of it` AT 91
-- (3) args: the opinion that the interests of justice warrant it, the investigation of the offence is continuing, a subsequent investigation is continuing
#ASSERT `s 196.1(3) the judge shall grant an extension of the 90-day period` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 196.1(3) the judge shall grant an extension of the 90-day period` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 196.1(3) the judge shall grant an extension of the 90-day period` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 196.1(3) the judge shall grant an extension of the 90-day period` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 196.1(3) the extension is within the limit` (`Length of time` OF 3 , 0 , 0 , FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 196.1(3) the extension is within the limit` (`Length of time` OF 3 , 0 , 1 , FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 196.1(4) the application meets the requirement of the subsection` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 196.1(4) the application meets the requirement of the subsection` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 196.1(4) the application meets the requirement of the subsection` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (5) args: the opinion, satisfied that the interception relates to an investigation of the offence, the offence, benefit of a group, criminal organization (s 2), terrorism offence (s 2)
-- (a): this list names 467.11, 467.12 and 467.13 and NOT 467.111 (finding 3); and it has the limb for the Foreign Interference and Security of Information Act
#ASSERT `s 196.1(5) the judge shall grant an extension of the 90-day period` TRUE TRUE (`s 195 test provision` `s 183 the Criminal Code` 467.11 "") FALSE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 196.1(5) the judge shall grant an extension of the 90-day period` TRUE TRUE (`s 195 test provision` `s 183 the Criminal Code` 467.12 "") FALSE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 196.1(5) the judge shall grant an extension of the 90-day period` TRUE TRUE (`s 195 test provision` `s 183 the Criminal Code` 467.13 "") FALSE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 196.1(5) the judge shall grant an extension of the 90-day period` TRUE TRUE (`s 195 test provision` `s 183 the Criminal Code` 52.1 "") FALSE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 196.1(5) the judge shall grant an extension of the 90-day period` TRUE TRUE (`s 195 test provision` `s 183 the Criminal Code` 467.111 "") FALSE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 196.1(5) the judge shall grant an extension of the 90-day period` TRUE TRUE (`s 195 test provision` `s 183 the Foreign Interference and Security of Information Act` 20.3 "(1)") FALSE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 196.1(5) the judge shall grant an extension of the 90-day period` TRUE TRUE (`s 195 test provision` `s 183 the Criminal Code` 380 "") TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 196.1(5) the judge shall grant an extension of the 90-day period` TRUE TRUE (`s 195 test provision` `s 183 the Criminal Code` 380 "") FALSE (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 196.1(5) the judge shall grant an extension of the 90-day period` TRUE TRUE (`s 195 test provision` `s 183 the Criminal Code` 380 "") FALSE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 196.1(5) the judge shall grant an extension of the 90-day period` FALSE TRUE (`s 195 test provision` `s 183 the Criminal Code` 52 "") FALSE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 196.1(5) the judge shall grant an extension of the 90-day period` TRUE FALSE (`s 195 test provision` `s 183 the Criminal Code` 52 "") FALSE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 196.1(5) the judge shall grant an extension of the 90-day period` TRUE TRUE (`s 195 test provision` `s 183 the Criminal Code` 380 "") TRUE NOTHING (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 196.1(5) the extension is within the limit` (`Length of time` OF 3 , 0 , 0 , FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 196.1(5) the extension is within the limit` (`Length of time` OF 3 , 0 , 1 , FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE

